WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.387
Unit 2 is the guide's Step 6.

2
00:00:02.387 --> 00:00:06.661
Network and Transport owns the
agency's own edge; inside Azure,

3
00:00:06.661 --> 00:00:11.688
Azure Firewall is the inspection point
for egress and east-west traffic.

4
00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:16.671
Learn's Zero Trust recommendations for
Azure Firewall check that outbound traffic

5
00:00:16.671 --> 00:00:19.305
from workloads routes
through the firewall,

6
00:00:19.305 --> 00:00:23.861
that threat intelligence and intrusion
detection are in alert-and-deny mode,

7
00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:27.563
that outbound TLS is inspected,
and that diagnostic logs are on.

8
00:00:27.563 --> 00:00:28.850
The SKU matters.

9
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:32.075
Threat intelligence deny
needs Standard or Premium.

10
00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:37.030
Intrusion detection and prevention,
TLS inspection and full URL filtering

11
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:42.300
need Premium, and Learn says Standard
upgrades to Premium without redeployment.

12
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:47.363
For high-volume egress, Learn suggests
a NAT gateway on the firewall subnet,

13
00:00:47.363 --> 00:00:49.813
to avoid running out of source ports.

14
00:00:49.813 --> 00:00:55.472
And TLS inspection needs an intermediate
C A certificate in Key Vault that clients

15
00:00:55.472 --> 00:01:01.100
trust; it doesn't decrypt the Education,
Finance, Government and Health categories.
